From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: aidl: primary: allow overriding output nominal latency via ro.vendor.audio.primary.out_latency_ms

ModulePrimary::getNominalLatencyMs() hardcodes 85 ms (4096 frames at 48 kHz)
for non-MMAP streams. Because AudioFlinger only enables FastMixer when the HAL
period is below 20 ms (kNormalPlaybackPeriodMs), low-latency AAudio/OpenSL ES
requests are rejected and end-to-end playback latency exceeds 300 ms.

Read ro.vendor.audio.primary.out_latency_ms for output streams in
ModulePrimary::getNominalLatencyMs() (keeping 85 ms when unset and leaving
capture streams at 85 ms). Setting the property to 10 ms yields a 480-frame
HAL transfer block and enables FastMixer on the primary output.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific tuning]
---
diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
index 4e16e84..cb6f23f 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #define LOG_TAG "AHAL_ModulePrimary"
 #include <Log.h>
 #include <Utils.h>
+#include <android-base/properties.h>
 
 #include "core-impl/Configuration.h"
 #include "core-impl/ModulePrimary.h"
@@ -192,7 +193,20 @@ int32_t ModulePrimary::getNominalLatencyMs(const AudioPortConfig& portConfig) {
     // the virtual Android device implementation to pass CTS. Hardware implementations
     // should have significantly lower latency.
     static constexpr int32_t kStandardLatencyMs = 85;
-    return hasMmapFlag(portConfig.flags.value()) ? kLowLatencyMs : kStandardLatencyMs;
+    if (hasMmapFlag(portConfig.flags.value())) return kLowLatencyMs;
+    // gaokun3: the playback block is what AudioFlinger sizes its mixer by. At 85 ms (4096 frames)
+    // there is no FastMixer (it starts only when the HAL buffer is shorter than the 20 ms normal
+    // sink, Threads.cpp kNormalPlaybackPeriodMs), FAST requests from games are denied, and a tap
+    // sound waits behind a 2-block client buffer + 85 ms + the ALSA buffer. Playback writes
+    // straight into ALSA and blocks there (StreamAlsaBase::transferPlaybackDirect()), so a small
+    // block only means more, shorter writes. The ALSA buffer holds a few periods of it, each rounded
+    // up to the q6apm-dai period step (applyOutputPeriodCount() in alsa/UtilsAlsa.cpp).
+    // Capture keeps 85 ms: its MonoPipe sizing and data-driven delivery were tuned for 4096.
+    if (portConfig.flags->getTag() == AudioIoFlags::output) {
+        return ::android::base::GetIntProperty("ro.vendor.audio.primary.out_latency_ms",
+                                               kStandardLatencyMs, 1, kStandardLatencyMs);
+    }
+    return kStandardLatencyMs;
 }
 
 ndk::ScopedAStatus ModulePrimary::getFlushFromFrameSupport(const AudioPortConfig& in_config,
